    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38205" root="متح" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاتِحٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَتُوحٌ</span></b>  <i>A drawer of water;</i> (S;)
applied to a man <i>who draws the water from the
mouth of the well:</i> one who draws it from the
bottom being called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَائِحٌ</span>: pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاتِحٌ</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَّاحٌ</span>.
(L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَاتِحٌ</span> A camel <i>that draws water:</i> pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَوَاتِحُ</span>. (L.) [See an ex. in a verse cited voce
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَمَّةٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">متُوحٌ</span>.

